# 🔒 Nexoin Vault

**Nexoin Vault** is a secure, lightweight, and local-first Android application designed to keep personal media, documents, and sensitive files private and safe from unauthorized access.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🔐 **Secure PIN & Password Access:** Passcode lock screen to prevent unauthorized access.
- 📁 **Private Media & File Storage:** Hide and manage private photos, videos, and documents.
- ⚡ **Local-First Privacy:** All encrypted assets stay strictly on your device — no cloud exposure.
- 🎨 **Clean & Intuitive Interface:** Smooth Material Design user experience tailored for ease of use.
- 🚀 **Fast Performance:** Optimized local database management and low resource footprint.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack & Requirements

| Layer | Technology / Tool |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Language** | Java / Kotlin |
| **IDE** | Android Studio (Ladybug / Jellyfish or higher) |
| **Min SDK** | API 24 (Android 7.0 Nougat) |
| **Target SDK** | API 34+ (Android 14) |
| **UI Design** | XML Layouts with Material Components |
| **Database/Storage** | SQLite / Room Database / Encrypted SharedPreferences |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Prerequisites
- [Android Studio](https://developer.android.com/studio) installed on your computer.
- Java Development Kit (JDK 17 or later).
- Android Device or Emulator running Android 7.0 (API level 24) or higher.

### 2. Installation & Setup

Clone the repository and open the project in Android Studio:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/asimhanan/Android_Studio.git](https://github.com/asimhanan/Android_Studio.git)
